  "title": "SMB2: Fix an array overflow",
  "description": "Fix\n\n```\n*** CID 1642679:  Insecure data handling  (TAINTED_SCALAR)\n/builds/wireshark/wireshark/epan/dissectors/packet-smb2.c: 12574 in dissect_smb2()\n12568     \t\t\toffset += 2;\n12569     \t\t}\n12570\n12571     \t\t/* opcode */\n12572     \t\tsi->opcode = tvb_get_letohs(tvb, offset);\n12573     \t\tproto_tree_add_item(header_tree, hf_smb2_cmd, tvb, offset, 2, ENC_LITTLE_ENDIAN);\n>>>     CID 1642679:  Insecure data handling  (TAINTED_SCALAR)\n>>>     Using tainted variable \"si->opcode\" as an index into an array \"smb2_cmd_vals\".\n12574     \t\tproto_item_append_text(item, \", %s %s\",\n12575     \t\t\tsmb2_cmd_vals[si->opcode].strptr,\n12576     \t\t\tsi->flags & SMB2_FLAGS_RESPONSE ? \"Response\" : \"Request\");\n12577     \t\toffset += 2;\n```\n\nand add a note about decode_smb2_name.\n\nFixes #20382",
